PRELIMINARY PLATS/PRELIMINARY ZONE CHANGES:
Preliminary Plat for Windmill Road, 2 Filing, a portion of the NE¼ of Section 28, T.14N.,
nd
R.66W., 6th P.M., Cheyenne, Wyoming (located at the southeast corner of the intersection of Dell
Range Boulevard and Windmill Road).” Jeff Wiggins, Parks and Recreation Department, reviewed past
history of the area and the proposed Greenway alignment for recreation and utilitarian purposes;
connectivity; safety incidents that have occurred at the intersection; proposed re-alignment of
Greenway path as outlined on the handout provided (on file in City Clerk’s office) with east-west
connectivity remaining the same, and possibility of future sale of land for commercial development.
Mr.  Brown moved to acknowledge receipt with staff recommendations #1 and 2 and Planning
Commission recommendation #3, seconded by Mr. Pierson.  Mr. Brown moved to remove Planning
Commission recommendation #3, seconded by Mr. Pierson, which reads as follows: City to retain
ownership of Lot 1, Block One for the greenway, as indicated on the preliminary plat map as submitted.
Brief discussion followed.  Motion to remove Planning Commission recommendation #3 carried.
Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body.  Comments of concern followed regarding the
possibility of declaring land as surplus, development of the land and whether the governing body has
the ability to place restrictions on what is eventually developed, and who would receive land sale
proceeds, if sold.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body with the
exception of Ms. Broyles, Ms. Case and Dr. Rinne voting “no”.
